## Why This Is Asked

Tests practical use of Cloud DLP and event-driven workflows, focusing on beginner-friendly integration, basic data protection, and observable outcomes via BigQuery.

## Key Concepts
- Cloud Storage event triggers
- Cloud DLP for secret detection
- Cloud Functions (event-driven) and simple orchestration
- Data routing to quarantine vs processed buckets
- BigQuery logging with deterministic insertId
- Idempotency and retries

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudocode for Cloud Function
exports.dlpScan = (event, context) => {
  const file = event.name;
  const result = dlp.inspect(file);
  const dest = result.secretsFound ? quarantinePath(file) : processedPath(file);
  copyTo(dest);
  logToBigQuery({ file, date: today(), secretsFound: result.secretsFound });
};
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test this with multiple concurrent uploads?
- How would you extend to handle multiple secret types and false positives?
